// The regex half of the ask.
//
// the Markdown dashboard §6 is an inventory of skills, guardrails and probes, hand-kept. §7 is the
// enforcement split, hand-kept. the coverage matrix is generated by grepping every
// probe's `--include='*.ext'` list. surface.retired.gen-doctrine-index scrapes frontmatter into a table
// and CI fails on a hand-edit inside the markers.
//
// All three are the same mechanism: read the ARTEFACTS with a pattern and hope the pattern
// still matches. None of them is versioned, so none can answer "what did 0.8.0 ship" — they
// answer "what is in the working tree right now", which is a different question wearing the
// same words.

thin-slice "TS.260821.07" {
    slug "publish-what-this-version-shipped"
    title "Publish the shipped doctrine for a version, derived from the record rather than scraped"
    kind "view"
    realizes "CAP.document-projection"
    from-storm "ES.260819.01"

    read-model "what-this-plugin-ships"
    actor "a reader deciding whether to adopt a version, and an adopter deciding whether to upgrade"
    needs-read-model "what-is-currently-true"

    trigger "somebody asks what a version shipped as doctrine, and the only answer available describes the working tree"
    outcome "the shipped surface set, its anchors, and its enforcement posture are published per version and regenerate identically"

    scenario #"""
        Given a record holding every shipped surface, what it serves, and which invariant each
             probe enforces
        When the set is published for a version
        Then it names every skill, guardrail, agent and probe that version shipped, what asked for
             each, and which gates fail closed — regenerated whole from the record, with no
             wall-clock stamp and no pattern applied to any Markdown file, because a document
             produced by grepping the tree is a document that describes whoever last ran it.
        """#

    step "1" does="the view is derived from doctrine-surface and invariant records — TS.260821.03 and TS.260821.05 already hold both"
    step "2" does="the enforcement posture is COMPUTED: which rules refuse, which report, which are witnessed, which invariants have an enforcer"
    step "3" does="language coverage is derived from what each probe declares, not from grepping its --include list"
    step "4" does="retire surface.retired.gen-coverage-matrix and surface.retired.gen-doctrine-index — a generator that greps is the fragility this replaces"
    step "5" does="the Markdown dashboard loses its inventory and enforcement sections and points at the published set"

    excludes "the whole of the Markdown dashboard. Its purpose, its opinions and its governance are \
        ARGUMENT, and generating an argument from state would be inventing one"
    excludes "retiring the probes themselves. They run in an adopter's CI against their languages, \
        which is exactly where a probe belongs"
    excludes "generating the README. The README is the plugin's working surface, read before anything \
        is installed and therefore not a projection of any version"

    layer "doctrine"    reaches="what a version shipped is stated by the record, and a hand-edit to the published copy is caught by verify-published"
    layer "enforcement" reaches="no generator applies a pattern to a Markdown file to learn what this plugin contains"
    layer "docs"        reaches="the archival projection carries the shipped set, and `what did 0.8.0 ship` stops being a question about the working tree"

    claim "C1" text="the shipped surface set for a version is derived from the record and regenerates byte-identically" \
        settled-by="publishing twice and comparing, plus verify-published against the commit the release names"
    claim "C2" text="the enforcement posture is computed, not restated — rules that refuse, rules that report, rules witnessed, invariants enforced" \
        settled-by="a test asserting each number comes from the checker and the prover, and that changing a rule's severity changes the published document"
    claim "C3" text="no published document is produced by matching a pattern against a Markdown file" \
        settled-by="the absence of surface.retired.gen-coverage-matrix and surface.retired.gen-doctrine-index, and a test that the publisher reads only the record"
    claim "C4" text="the set published for an older version still describes that version, not the tree" \
        settled-by="publishing two versions from one record and asserting they differ in the surfaces each shipped"

    depends-on "TS.260821.05 — a probe cannot say what it enforces until the invariant is a kind"
    depends-on "TS.260821.06 — the capability set is the other half of the same published tree"

    useful-alone "`what did 0.8.0 ship, and what of it fails closed` becomes answerable from the \
        record, for any version, at any time. Today it is answerable only for the working tree and \
        only by running four scripts"
    useful-to "the-reader-of-a-release" "the-adopter"

    attacks "S6"

    cut-from "the ask to regenerate docs/<version> from state rather than by regex"

    principle-note "the fragile thing about a regex over Markdown is not the regex. It is that the \
        prose was the state — so the pattern was the only reader, and the only way to find out it \
        had stopped matching was for somebody to notice the output looked wrong"

    proves "the doctrine a version shipped is recoverable from the record for that version"
    does-not-prove "that the doctrine was GOOD at that version. It says what shipped and what \
        enforced it, never whether either was worth shipping"
}
